{{!
    Override of core_form/element-date_time_selector.

    Identical to lib/form/templates/element-date_time_selector.mustache except
    that the  between the group's elements is dropped.

    Why: lib/form/group.php emits a literal `&nbsp;` between elements. The row is
    a flex container, so each of those text nodes becomes an anonymous flex item
    with a width of its own AND a `gap` on either side — spacing that can be
    neither targeted nor removed from CSS. On the Course Settings embed it made
    the dropdown spacing uneven, and on an optional date (Course end date) the
    separator trailing the "Enable" checkbox landed at the head of the wrapped
    line, indenting that row past the row above it.

    With the separators gone, the flex `gap` in post.scss is the single source of
    the spacing and every date row lines up. Structure only — the elements, their
    order, the fieldset, and the accessible legend are untouched.
}}
{{< core_form/element-group }}
    {{$element}}
        <fieldset data-fieldtype="date_time" class="m-0 p-0 border-0" id="{{element.id}}">
            <legend class="visually-hidden">{{label}}</legend>
            <div class="fdate_time_selector d-flex flex-wrap align-items-center">
            {{#element.elements}}
                {{{html}}}
            {{/element.elements}}
            </div>
        </fieldset>
    {{/element}}
{{/ core_form/element-group }}
